course: dictionary
lesson: 4512
title: Headache: a pain or a problem
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A headache is a pain in your head. The word can also mean a problem that is annoying or hard to solve, as in «Fixing the broken bike gave Sam a real headache.» To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. Are they about being ill, or about something that is hard to do?
explain: «Flu comes on suddenly with high fever, aching muscles, headache, shivers and great tiredness.» The other words are about being ill, so headache here is the pain in the head. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Headaches often have causes you can avoid. «A boy in Arizona played football all afternoon in the heat without drinking; he got a headache, felt dizzy and had to be cooled down.» Not drinking enough, too much sun, not sleeping enough, too much screen time and being hungry can all cause a headache.
explain: If you get a headache, rest, drink some water and tell an adult. Only an adult should give you medicine for a headache. A very bad headache with a stiff neck, a rash, or one that comes after a head bump needs a doctor straight away.
fact: A headache is a pain in your head.
fact: «Headache» can also mean a problem that is annoying or hard to solve.
fact: Common causes of headaches include not drinking enough water, not sleeping enough, too much screen time and being hungry.
fact: Tell an adult if you have a headache, and only an adult should give you headache medicine.
fact: Get a doctor straight away for a very bad headache with a stiff neck, a rash, or one that comes after a bump to the head.
exercise: What is a headache? | A long walk | A type of bread | A kind of hat | *A pain in your head
exercise: «Fixing the bike gave Sam a real headache.» What does headache mean here? | *A problem that is hard to solve | A sore foot | A broken bell | A pain in Sam's head from the sun
exercise: Mia has a headache. What should she do first? | Ignore it and say nothing | Play football until it goes away | Take medicine from her own bag | *Rest, drink some water and tell an adult
test: «A boy in Australia did not drink anything on a long, hot hike; he got a headache, felt sick and nearly fainted.» What most likely caused his headache? | Learning to swim | *Not drinking enough water in the heat | Too much sleep | Eating too many vegetables
test: Which of these needs a doctor straight away? | A headache after a quiet afternoon reading | A small headache after a long day at school | A headache after drinking a glass of water | *A very bad headache with a stiff neck and a rash
exam: Which sentence uses headache to mean a problem? | The boy's headache went away after a nap. | I have a headache, so I will lie down. | Mum gave me water for my headache. | *The maths puzzle was a real headache for the whole class.
